  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-independent-bnpl-title (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads a platform-specific second-stage binary and executes it in the background. It fetches the payload over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev and oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac and /pkg/package.exe, with a DNS TXT-based fallback channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru per platform). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and spawned detached (cmd.exe start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"\u0026\" on Unix) so it runs in the background. The package name impersonates the Dolyame BNPL service.",
